BUSINESS METRICS:

Lead-to-opportunity rate:

Opportunities / Eligible leads × 100

Conversion rate:

Converted leads / Eligible leads × 100

Win rate:

Won opportunities / Closed opportunities × 100

Follow-up completion rate:

Completed tasks / Eligible tasks × 100

Pipeline value:

Sum of eligible open opportunity values.

Ensure denominators are clearly defined.

MACHINE LEARNING METRICS:

- Precision.
- Recall.
- F1-score.
- ROC-AUC.
- PR-AUC.
- Confusion matrix.

Requirements:

- Create a leakage-safe training and test split.
- Prefer chronological evaluation.
- Keep future outcomes out of training features.
- Exclude ground truth anomaly labels from predictive features.
- Use only features available at prediction time.
- Report class imbalance.
- Handle undefined metrics safely.
- Explain model limitations.
- Compare rule-based scoring with predictive model performance.

Do not fabricate model metrics.

If a predictive model has not been trained, report NOT TRAINED rather than displaying invented results.

